    "poster_id": 933348,
    "post_rendered": "Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/1/9b18bf5d62cddd22019c46fb286d4a48b72355db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"\\( a_n \\)\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" > be a sequence of positive real numbers such that for every <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/d/45dff2716b6a07268983215d10aa334618fca20b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"\\( n &gt; 2025 \\)\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"73\" height=\"15\" >,</span> we have:<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/0/e30e9e533eb9a41cf847484e676ac4522edda665.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\na_n = \\max_{1 \\leq i \\leq 2025} a_{n-i} - \\min_{1 \\leq i \\leq 2025} a_{n-i}\n\\]\"  width=\"254\" height=\"25\" >Prove that there exists a natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/e/39e72e2ae7da55d37cda657f6dd345c335b2397f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"\\( M \\)\"  width=\"19\" height=\"12\" > such that for all <span style=\"white-space:pre;\"><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/c/cfcb6535ad39b01b64109d5a21e2f204d10f59ac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"\\( n &gt; M \\)\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"57\" height=\"15\" >,</span> the following holds:<br>\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01f1a81eed2230332d51a15501ef2a6ad3a7ec82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\na_n &lt; \\frac{1}{1404}\n\\]\"  width=\"80\" height=\"37\" ><i>Proposed by Navid Safaei</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Let \\( a_n \\) be a sequence of positive real numbers such that for every \\( n > 2025 \\), we have:\n\\[\na_n = \\max_{1 \\leq i \\leq 2025} a_{n-i} - \\min_{1 \\leq i \\leq 2025} a_{n-i}\n\\]\nProve that there exists a natural number \\( M \\) such that for all \\( n > M \\), the following holds:\n\\[\na_n < \\frac{1}{1404}\n\\]\n[i]Proposed by Navid Safaei[/i]",
