   "post_data": {
    "post_id": 34960128,
    "post_type": "forum",
    "topic_id": 3580172,
    "poster_id": 933348,
    "post_rendered": "Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/3/15398e191a479087913c6291e869faf7ae4d0126.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"\\( n &gt; 10 \\)\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" > lines are drawn on the plane such that no three of them are concurrent and no two are parallel. At least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7eea58938abc957ad652d54edeb41132d6bb23d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"\\( \\frac{n^2}{8} + 1 \\)\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"52\" height=\"26\" > of the bounded regions formed are colored black. A triangle formed by three lines is called a \\textit{good triangle} if it lies entirely within a black region. Prove that there are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/7/847cf8ab5e0ca06245b4ea8ae68cb923577251ad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"\\( \\frac{n}{2} \\)\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"14\" height=\"20\" > good triangles. (A good triangle is a bounded region with finite area.)<br>\n<br>\n<i>Proposed by Mehran Talaei</i>",
    "post_canonical": "Suppose \\( n > 10 \\) lines are drawn on the plane such that no three of them are concurrent and no two are parallel. At least \\( \\frac{n^2}{8} + 1 \\) of the bounded regions formed are colored black. A triangle formed by three lines is called a \\textit{good triangle} if it lies entirely within a black region. Prove that there are at least \\( \\frac{n}{2} \\) good triangles. (A good triangle is a bounded region with finite area.)\n\n[i]Proposed by Mehran Talaei[/i]",
